Robert R Schneck wrote:

> The other main thing is to gather all the piddly armor---orcish helms,
> etc---that you'd really rather just ignore.  Eventually you'll find
> something nicely enchanted.

If you want to try on _lots_ of "piddly armor", you'd do well to altarize it 
first.  Often, when I've just wiped out a barracks, I'll grab all the 
helmets, gloves and boots that I can find and drag them to the nearest 
altar.

My own rule for early armor gathering is to try it on if it isn't possibly 
something harmful such as gauntlets of fumbling, and if it will improve my 
AC assuming +0 enchantment.  Exceptions can be made for spellcasting and 
encumbrance.


